<!--
  Served at https://electra.academy/sitemap.xml.

  Only the canonical root form of each URL is listed. The same pages are also
  reachable under /home/... and with an explicit /index.html, because
  home/server/index.js mounts the directory twice - those variants carry a
  rel=canonical pointing here and must not appear in this file.

  Kept by hand: nine pages, and no build step exists that could generate it.

  No <lastmod>, <changefreq> or <priority> on purpose. Google ignores the latter
  two outright, and a <lastmod> nobody keeps accurate is worse than none - once it
  is provably stale the crawler stops trusting it. Add it back only together with
  something that maintains it.

  The apps are listed WITH a trailing slash: /simulator would earn a 301 from the
  ingress canonicaliser, and a sitemap should not point at redirects.
-->
